Mi Pad 2 camera support

This package installs the early platform-helper module load list, a modprobe
soft dependency that loads the camera sensors and VCM before the AtomISP PCI
driver, and the Intel IPU/AtomISP 2401 firmware. It expects the custom mipad2
kernel modules to be installed under /usr/lib/modules.

The AtomISP graph exposes both OV5693 (front) and T4KA3 (rear). The rear
T4KA3 automatically instantiates its DW9761 VCM at address 0x0c.

The firmware is installed at /usr/lib/firmware/intel/ipu/shisp_2401a0_v21.bin.
The load-order rule follows the Mi Pad 2 Android init configuration, which
explicitly warns that AtomISP must load after its sensor drivers:
https://github.com/latte-dev/android_device_xiaomi_latte/blob/cm-13.0/ramdisk/init.latte.rc
No Wi-Fi or Bluetooth firmware is included or changed by this package.
